   "source": [
    "### Reading the Phase Diagram\n",
    "\n",
    "- The **purple line** ($\\dot{k} = 0$) shows combinations of $k$ and $c$ where capital is neither accumulating nor decumulating.\n",
    "- The **orange vertical line** ($\\dot{c} = 0$ at $k^*$) shows where consumption growth is zero. In the AK model this is degenerate — $f'(k) = A$ for all $k$, so this becomes a parameter condition rather than a state-dependent locus.\n",
    "- The **blue path** is the unique saddle path from $(k_0, c_0)$ to $(k^*, c^*)$.\n",
    "- Off-path trajectories (green/red) diverge: they do not converge to the steady state.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
